{
  "schema_version": "1.0",
  "encounter_id": "00252",
  "segments": [
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0001",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 1.2,
      "end_seconds": 7.37,
      "duration_seconds": 6.17,
      "text": "Hmm, doctor, hello, I've got my papers here, where should I put them?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0002",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 8.06,
      "end_seconds": 10.7,
      "duration_seconds": 2.64,
      "text": "Yes, do sit. Tell me what's been happening."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0003",
      "speaker_id": "person_3",
      "role": "CAREGIVER",
      "start_seconds": 12.23,
      "end_seconds": 21.34,
      "duration_seconds": 9.11,
      "text": "Thank you for fitting us in, uh, doctor. Doctor, you know, it's pain in both knees. That's what we're worried about."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0004",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 22.51,
      "end_seconds": 27.04,
      "duration_seconds": 4.53,
      "text": "How long have you had it? I'm asking so that we don't miss anything."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0005",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 28.03,
      "end_seconds": 41.07,
      "duration_seconds": 13.04,
      "text": "Uh, uh, it's been going on for two months. I thought it would sort itself out, but it hasn't. I kept putting it off, which I know isn't sensible."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0006",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 42.46,
      "end_seconds": 44.33,
      "duration_seconds": 1.87,
      "text": "And how severe is it?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0007",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 45.21,
      "end_seconds": 49.71,
      "duration_seconds": 4.5,
      "text": "A seven out of ten, uh, I suppose."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0008",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 50.22,
      "end_seconds": 51.18,
      "duration_seconds": 0.96,
      "text": "Anything that helps?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0009",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 51.72,
      "end_seconds": 55.8,
      "duration_seconds": 4.08,
      "text": "It settles a little with a hot pack and rest."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0010",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 57.12,
      "end_seconds": 60.15,
      "duration_seconds": 3.03,
      "text": "What's the pattern, is it there all day?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0011",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 62.91,
      "end_seconds": 65.63,
      "duration_seconds": 2.72,
      "text": "I'd say once or twice a day."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0012",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 66.23,
      "end_seconds": 69.74,
      "duration_seconds": 3.51,
      "text": "Any difficulty getting up from a chair as well?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0013",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 73.68,
      "end_seconds": 87.43,
      "duration_seconds": 13.75,
      "text": "Yes, um, I have. Uh, and there's swelling in the right knee as well, about a month now. With swelling in the right knee, only elevation, and it's not much."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0014",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 87.83,
      "end_seconds": 91.97,
      "duration_seconds": 4.14,
      "text": "Any redness over the knee, fever or pain in other joints at all?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0015",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 92.42,
      "end_seconds": 97.97,
      "duration_seconds": 5.55,
      "text": "No, no redness over the knee, fever or pain in other joints."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0016",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 98.5,
      "end_seconds": 102.0,
      "duration_seconds": 3.5,
      "text": "Have you been able to keep up with your usual activities?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0017",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 105.76,
      "end_seconds": 118.29,
      "duration_seconds": 12.53,
      "text": "For the most part, yes. I just carry on and try not to dwell on things too much, though I won't pretend it hasn't crossed my mind a few times."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0018",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 121.19,
      "end_seconds": 124.09,
      "duration_seconds": 2.9,
      "text": "Let's go through your medication. What are you taking?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0019",
      "speaker_id": "person_3",
      "role": "CAREGIVER",
      "start_seconds": 125.16,
      "end_seconds": 138.51,
      "duration_seconds": 13.35,
      "text": "Oh, you know, she takes Glycomet, 500 milligrams, twice a day. I mean, you know, she is on paracetamol, 500 milligrams, when needed, I give it to her."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0020",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 139.2,
      "end_seconds": 144.51,
      "duration_seconds": 5.31,
      "text": "Do you have any known allergies at all? I'll explain everything as we go along."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0021",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 145.39,
      "end_seconds": 149.32,
      "duration_seconds": 3.93,
      "text": "So, you know, no, none that I know of."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0022",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 150.36,
      "end_seconds": 154.23,
      "duration_seconds": 3.87,
      "text": "Do you have any medical conditions, anything you've been treated for?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0023",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 155.25,
      "end_seconds": 161.94,
      "duration_seconds": 6.69,
      "text": "I've had diabetes for five years now. Sorry, I know I'm rambling a bit."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0024",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 163.15,
      "end_seconds": 166.2,
      "duration_seconds": 3.05,
      "text": "Sorry, the computer needs a moment to load this."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0025",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 166.54,
      "end_seconds": 167.41,
      "duration_seconds": 0.87,
      "text": "No rush."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0026",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 180.42,
      "end_seconds": 181.88,
      "duration_seconds": 1.46,
      "text": "Alright, I've got it."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0027",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 182.9,
      "end_seconds": 185.23,
      "duration_seconds": 2.33,
      "text": "Okay, let's do a quick examination."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0028",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 185.79,
      "end_seconds": 187.08,
      "duration_seconds": 1.29,
      "text": "Okay, go ahead."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0029",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 188.06,
      "end_seconds": 190.29,
      "duration_seconds": 2.23,
      "text": "I'll just listen to your chest now."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0030",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 204.42,
      "end_seconds": 208.97,
      "duration_seconds": 4.55,
      "text": "Bending is limited to about a right angle, and it hurts at the end."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0031",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 209.79,
      "end_seconds": 211.57,
      "duration_seconds": 1.78,
      "text": "Bear with me a second."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0032",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 225.2,
      "end_seconds": 231.12,
      "duration_seconds": 5.92,
      "text": "There's mild swelling on the right knee, and a grating feel when I bend it."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0033",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 233.44,
      "end_seconds": 257.66,
      "duration_seconds": 24.22,
      "text": "That's fine, you can get dressed. Thank you for that. I'll write up what I found in a moment, and then I'll tell you what I think is going on. What I'm doing here is putting together three things: what you tell me, what I find when I examine you, and what the tests show. None of those alone is enough, which is why we sometimes need to wait for results before being certain."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0034",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 258.1,
      "end_seconds": 260.57,
      "duration_seconds": 2.47,
      "text": "Oh, I appreciate you explaining that."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0035",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 261.45,
      "end_seconds": 271.13,
      "duration_seconds": 9.68,
      "text": "Right, here's what I'm thinking. It fits best with osteoarthritis of the knees. It could also be an inflammatory arthritis, so we'll keep that open."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0036",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 272.6,
      "end_seconds": 275.02,
      "duration_seconds": 2.42,
      "text": "Is it something serious, doctor?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0037",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 276.09,
      "end_seconds": 290.52,
      "duration_seconds": 14.43,
      "text": "Nothing I've seen today points to an emergency. It looks like osteoarthritis of the knees, but I'd like to confirm. Let me just recap so I've got it right. You've had pain in both knees for two months, and no fever or redness over the knee."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0038",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 291.37,
      "end_seconds": 293.06,
      "duration_seconds": 1.69,
      "text": "Yes, you've got it."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0039",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 294.11,
      "end_seconds": 298.3,
      "duration_seconds": 4.19,
      "text": "Let me make a quick note of that before I forget."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0040",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 299.11,
      "end_seconds": 299.81,
      "duration_seconds": 0.7,
      "text": "Okay."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0041",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 312.89,
      "end_seconds": 342.25,
      "duration_seconds": 29.36,
      "text": "Alright, I've got it. We should do blood tests for joint pain. It's a routine test and it'll give us a much clearer picture. We should do an X-ray of both knees for knee pain. I'd rather check than guess, and this is the quickest way to know more. Let's use etoricoxib, 60 milligrams, once a day, for five days. That should help with knee pain. It's a commonly used medicine and most people tolerate it well."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0042",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 342.92,
      "end_seconds": 346.56,
      "duration_seconds": 3.64,
      "text": "Well, alright, I'll pick it up today."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0043",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 347.04,
      "end_seconds": 374.3,
      "duration_seconds": 27.26,
      "text": "Losing even a few kilos takes a lot of load off the knees, and I'd like you to do the strengthening exercises. Cut down on salt and fried food for now, it really does make a difference. Make sure you're drinking plenty of fluids, two to three litres a day if you can, and get proper rest. I want you to come back or go to emergency straight away if the symptoms get worse."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0044",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 375.62,
      "end_seconds": 377.66,
      "duration_seconds": 2.04,
      "text": "Got it, thank you."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0045",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 378.82,
      "end_seconds": 382.22,
      "duration_seconds": 3.4,
      "text": "I'd like to see you again in six weeks."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0046",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 383.78,
      "end_seconds": 384.48,
      "duration_seconds": 0.7,
      "text": "Alright."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0047",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 385.34,
      "end_seconds": 390.9,
      "duration_seconds": 5.56,
      "text": "Tell me what you've taken from all that, so I can fill in any gaps."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0048",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 391.88,
      "end_seconds": 400.63,
      "duration_seconds": 8.75,
      "text": "So, I take the etoricoxib, 60 milligrams, once a day and come back in six weeks. Is that right?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0049",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 401.62,
      "end_seconds": 405.93,
      "duration_seconds": 4.31,
      "text": "Yes, exactly right. Take care, and don't hesitate to call if anything changes."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0050",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 407.24,
      "end_seconds": 411.65,
      "duration_seconds": 4.41,
      "text": "I, I think that's clear. Thank you for being so thorough."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0051",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 412.25,
      "end_seconds": 413.22,
      "duration_seconds": 0.97,
      "text": "See you then."
    }
  ]
}